post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
smckbd is built by DKMS for every installed kernel 7.3 and newer. Older
kernels keep applesmc, which already provides smc::kbd_backlight.

The unit is enabled but not started here: the DKMS hook may not have built the
module yet. Start it once, or reboot:
  sudo systemctl start smckbd.service

Check it:
  ls -l /sys/class/leds/ | grep kbd_backlight
  echo 120 | sudo tee /sys/class/leds/smc::kbd_backlight/brightness
EOF

  if [ -d /run/systemd/system ]; then
    systemctl enable smckbd.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  fi
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  if [ -d /run/systemd/system ]; then
    systemctl disable --now smckbd.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  fi
}
